op retention (under the M8 nyloc nut). Origin = bearing face centre, +
Z away from the prop.',(#401953));
#402008=PRODUCT('HW_Nut_M8_Nyloc_DIN985','HW_Nut_M8_Nyloc_DIN985 v1',
'M8 nyloc (prevailing-torque) lock nut DIN 985, A2 stainless + nylon i
nsert: AF 13, h 8. Pusher prop lock on the VT 4130 prop adapter. Origi
n = bearing face centre, +Z away from the prop.',(#401953));
#402009=PRODUCT('51_VTOL_Unit','51_VTOL_Unit',$,(#401953));
#402010=PRODUCT('COTS_Motor_VT8020PRO_120KV',
'COTS_Motor_VT8020PRO_120KV v1',
'Vector Technics VT 8020 PRO 120 KV VTOL motor, 12S. Outer shape from 
datasheet 2D CAD p.1: \X\D888.4, 40.5 to bell top, \X\D829 x 2 hub, \X\D8
8 x 5.9 shaft (42.5 + 5.9 = 48.4 over shaft). Base mount 4x M4 x10 on 
PCD 40 at 45\X\B0; prop mount 4x M3 PCD 20 at 45\X\B0 + 4x M4 PCD 23 a
t 0/90\X\B0, depth 8. Phase wires exit radially at +X, Z 4.2 above mou
nt face. Origin = mount face centre, +Z toward prop. Mass 566 g (body 
density tuned).',(#401953));
#402011=PRODUCT('FAB_VTOL_Motor_Mount_v5','FAB_VTOL_Motor_Mount_v5 v3',

'SAGE VTOL motor mount v5 (Al 6061 CNC, hard-anodised), single piece, 
after the Motor Arm Set reference: full collar on the d45 boom with a 
bottom slot and 2 pinch-tab pairs (M3 horizontal, from outside); drum 
body + d56 motor plate with d15 pilot for the VT 8020 base recess and 
kidney windows; 4x d8 long-driver access holes in the collar under the
 4x M4 x10 motor screws (motor bolted with the mount off the boom); si
de windows; d4 side index-pin hole (into a jig-drilled boom hole on th
e neutral axis: roll + boom station); +X tail with wire tray (3 inline
 4 mm bullets) and d8 drop hole; screw-on tray lid (2x M2.5 from the t
op). Frame = 51_VTOL_Unit. Strobe wiring: grommeted d5 hole each side 
of the drum (x 0, z 14) for the StrobeIT lead, d4 channel through the 
web (z 19) into the wire tray; the lead joins the phase wires down the
 d8 drop hole.',(#401953));
#402012=PRODUCT('60_Avionics_Payload','60_Avionics_Payload',$,(#401953));
#402013=PRODUCT('61_Battery_R','61_Battery_R',
'Battery bay R: linked BATT_12S_Cartridge_R (slides along Y on an as-b
uilt slider joint) + BATT_Bay_Receptacle_R (floating blade receptacle 
in the liner pocket).',(#401953));
#402014=PRODUCT('BATT_Bay_Receptacle_R','BATT_Bay_Receptacle_R v2',
'SAGE battery-bay blade receptacle (R side), mates with BATT_12S_Cartr
idge_R. PA66-GF30 housing 18.5 x 9.75 x 24.5 in the CF liner pocket (X
 63-83, Y +252-294, Z +-13), 0.75 mm float all round, located by 2 ver
tical M3 shoulder screws (d4 shoulder) through d5.5 holes in the pocke
t top/bottom walls + wave washers. 2 louvered Cu-Be Ag-plated sockets 
for the 1.6 x 18 blades (POS fwd slot, NEG aft slot), 4 Au pogo pins (
SMBus data/clock, NTC, ID) onto the plug pads. POS 8 AWG exits up and 
NEG 8 AWG exits down through d9 holes in the pocket walls, signal lead
 up (d3.6). Frame = aircraft axes.',(#401953));
#402015=PRODUCT('BATT_12S_Cartridge_R','BATT_12S_Cartridge_R v1',
'SAGE 12S battery cartridge (R side), side-loaded into the CF liner at
 Y +255..388. Envelope 148 x 110 x 114 (pack), 2.85 kg pack. Pack: 12S
1P LiPo pouch (assumed ~10 Ah, 444 Wh; cells TBD) - 12 cells 10.2 x 93
 x 107 mm (+ seal flanges, Al/Ni tabs) on 0.8 mm EVA interleaves, G10 
end plates, FR4 balance/BMS board with Ni-plated Cu busbars at the inn
er end, 8 AWG silicone main leads + SMBus/balance lead in a 9 mm chann
el at the fwd end, PVC wrap. Case: PA-12 MJF 2 mm shell with lead-in c
hamfers, 2 integral cantilever snap latches (top/bottom, 1.8 x 10 x 40
 mm arm, 1.5 mm hook: 26.6 deg insertion ramp + square catch into the 
12 x 6 liner window at X 155-167 / Y 349-355), release tabs in 16 mm t
humb recesses, outer cap with the flush fuselage-OML face + pull-grip 
cup, lap-joint lip (bonded + 4x M2.5), UHMW-PE 0.5 mm slide pads. Blad
e plug: PA66-GF30 housing in the case boss, 2 Ag-plated Cu blades 1.6 
x 18 (POS fwd, NEG aft), 4 Au signal pads (SMBus, temp, ID). Mates wit
h BATT_Bay_Receptacle_R (floating, in the liner pocket). Frame = aircr
aft axes.',(#401953));
